WEBVTT

00:02.480 --> 00:04.815
Water...

00:05.358 --> 00:07.025
Earth...

00:07.652 --> 00:09.611
Fire...

00:09.904 --> 00:12.114
Air.

00:13.157 --> 00:16.576
My grandmother used to
tell me stories about the old days.

00:16.661 --> 00:18.245
A time of peace,

00:18.329 --> 00:20.998
when the Avatar kept balance
between Water Tribes,

00:21.082 --> 00:22.791
Earth Kingdom, Fire Nation,

00:22.875 --> 00:24.501
and Air Nomads.

00:24.585 --> 00:27.504
But that all changed
when the Fire Nation attacked.

00:31.467 --> 00:35.012
Only the Avatar
mastered all four elements.

00:35.096 --> 00:38.557
Only he could stop
the ruthless firebenders.

00:38.641 --> 00:41.435
But when the world needed him most,
he vanished.

00:44.355 --> 00:46.064
A hundred years have passed,

00:46.149 --> 00:48.942
and the Fire Nation
is nearing victory in the war.

00:50.111 --> 00:52.446
Two years ago, my father
and the men of my tribe

00:52.530 --> 00:55.949
journeyed to the Earth Kingdom
to help fight against the Fire Nation,

00:56.034 --> 00:58.827
leaving me and my brother
to look after our tribe.

00:59.996 --> 01:03.874
Some people believe that the Avatar
Was never reborn into the Air Nomads,

01:03.958 --> 01:05.584
and that the cycle is broken.

01:06.002 --> 01:07.627
But I haven't lost hope.

01:08.004 --> 01:09.629
I still believe that somehow

01:09.714 --> 01:12.883
the Avatar will return to save the world.

01:58.096 --> 02:00.055
It's not getting away from me this time.

02:00.348 --> 02:01.515
Watch and learn, Katara.

02:01.891 --> 02:03.350
This is how you catch a fish.

02:13.945 --> 02:15.320
Sokka, look!

02:15.613 --> 02:17.239
Shh, Katara.

02:17.323 --> 02:19.324
You're gonna scare him away.

02:19.409 --> 02:21.326
I can already smell it cooking.

02:21.911 --> 02:24.246
But, Sokka, I caught one.

02:26.207 --> 02:27.374
Hey!

02:27.458 --> 02:28.708
Aah!

02:29.127 --> 02:30.794
Why is it that every time

02:30.878 --> 02:32.504
you play with magic water,

02:32.588 --> 02:33.964
I get soaked?

02:35.133 --> 02:37.634
It's not magic. It's waterbending.

02:37.718 --> 02:38.802
And it's--

02:38.886 --> 02:41.263
Yeah, yeah. An ancient art
unique to our culture,

02:41.347 --> 02:42.347
Blah, blah, blah...

02:42.432 --> 02:44.766
Look, I'm just saying that
if I had weird powers,

02:44.851 --> 02:46.393
I'd keep my weirdness to myself.

02:46.477 --> 02:48.270
You're calling me weird?

02:48.438 --> 02:50.647
I'm not the one
who makes muscles at myself

02:50.731 --> 02:53.358
every time I see my reflection
in the water.

03:09.208 --> 03:10.500
Watch out!

03:11.586 --> 03:12.669
-Aah!
-Go left!

03:12.753 --> 03:13.837
Go left!

03:17.425 --> 03:20.927
Aah!

03:25.808 --> 03:27.058
You call that left?

03:27.143 --> 03:28.560
You don't like my steering.

03:28.644 --> 03:31.813
Well, maybe you should have
waterbended us out of the ice.

03:31.981 --> 03:34.649
-So it's my fault.
-I knew I should have left you home.

03:35.109 --> 03:36.985
Leave it to a girl to screw things up.

03:39.238 --> 03:43.450
You are the most sexist, immature,
nutbrained--

03:43.701 --> 03:46.161
I'm embarrassed to be related to you!

03:48.956 --> 03:51.917
Ever since mom died, I've been doing
all the work around camp,

03:52.001 --> 03:53.835
while you've been off playing soldier.

03:54.045 --> 03:55.545
Katara...

03:55.630 --> 03:57.589
I even wash all the clothes!

03:57.673 --> 04:00.383
Have you ever smelled your dirty socks?

04:00.510 --> 04:01.635
Let me tell you.

04:01.719 --> 04:03.011
Not pleasant!

04:03.346 --> 04:05.138
Katara! Settle down!

04:05.223 --> 04:08.058
No! That's it. I'm done helping you.

04:08.267 --> 04:10.644
From now on, you're on your own!

04:24.450 --> 04:27.410
Okay. You've gone from weird
to freakish, Katara.

04:27.495 --> 04:29.204
You mean, I did that?

04:29.288 --> 04:31.831
Yep. Congratulations.

05:03.739 --> 05:06.491
He's alive. We have to help.

05:06.576 --> 05:08.618
Katara! Get back here!

05:08.911 --> 05:10.537
We don't know what that thing is.

05:44.363 --> 05:45.739
Finally.

05:45.948 --> 05:48.366
Uncle, do you realize what this means?

05:48.743 --> 05:50.869
I won't get to finish my game?

05:51.078 --> 05:53.663
It means my search
is about to come to an end.

05:56.834 --> 05:59.586
That light came from
an incredibly powerful source.

05:59.670 --> 06:00.920
It has to be him.

06:01.255 --> 06:04.049
Or it's just the celestial lights.

06:04.258 --> 06:06.968
We've been down this road before,
Prince Zuko.

06:07.178 --> 06:10.597
I don't want you
to get too excited over nothing.

06:11.766 --> 06:13.350
Please, sit.

06:13.559 --> 06:18.021
Why don't you enjoy
a cup of calming jasmine tea?

06:18.356 --> 06:20.190
I don't need any calming tea!

06:20.274 --> 06:22.067
I need to capture the Avatar!

06:22.276 --> 06:24.861
Helmsman, head a course for the light.

06:44.382 --> 06:45.548
Stop!

07:01.982 --> 07:03.108
Stop it!

07:14.954 --> 07:17.288
I need to ask you something.

07:17.373 --> 07:18.540
What?

07:18.708 --> 07:20.834
Please, come closer.

07:21.001 --> 07:22.210
What is it?

07:23.546 --> 07:25.338
Will you go penguin-sailing with me?

07:25.798 --> 07:27.632
Sure.

07:27.925 --> 07:29.092
I guess.

07:30.344 --> 07:32.178
What's going on here?

07:32.263 --> 07:33.388
You tell us!

07:33.472 --> 07:35.056
How did you get in the ice?

07:35.141 --> 07:36.433
And why aren't you frozen?

07:36.851 --> 07:37.892
I'm not sure.

07:45.401 --> 07:47.652
Appa, are you all right?

07:48.070 --> 07:50.488
Wake up, buddy.

07:59.540 --> 08:02.417
Ha ha! You're okay.

08:08.174 --> 08:09.549
What is that thing?

08:09.675 --> 08:11.217
This is Appa, my flying bison.

08:11.302 --> 08:14.262
Right. And this is Katara,
my flying sister.

08:18.184 --> 08:20.643
Look out!

08:26.734 --> 08:28.151
Don't worry. It'll wash out.

08:30.863 --> 08:32.530
So, do you guys live around here?

08:32.907 --> 08:35.533
Don't answer that.
Did you see that crazy bolt of light?

08:35.618 --> 08:37.869
He was probably trying
to signal the Fire Navy.

08:37.953 --> 08:40.246
Yeah.
I'm sure he's a spy for the Fire Navy.

08:40.331 --> 08:43.249
You can tell by that evil look in his eye.

08:45.169 --> 08:47.378
The paranoid one is my brother Sokka.

08:47.630 --> 08:49.130
You never told us your name.

08:49.632 --> 08:51.466
I'm-- Ah! Ah!

08:54.845 --> 08:57.263
Ah-choo!

09:04.063 --> 09:06.064
I'm Aang.

09:07.107 --> 09:10.318
You just sneezed
and flew ten feet in the air.

09:10.402 --> 09:11.986
Really? It felt higher than that.

09:12.571 --> 09:14.197
You're an airbender.

09:14.490 --> 09:15.657
Sure am.

09:15.741 --> 09:18.326
Giant light beams,
flying bison, airbenders--

09:18.410 --> 09:20.245
I think I got midnight sun madness.

09:20.538 --> 09:22.539
I'm going home to where stuff makes sense.

09:26.877 --> 09:30.129
Well, if you guys are stuck,
Appa and I can give you a lift.

09:33.425 --> 09:35.009
We'd love a ride, thanks.

09:35.261 --> 09:38.638
No! I am not getting
on that fluffy snot monster.

09:38.764 --> 09:41.641
Are you hoping some other
kind of monster will come along

09:41.725 --> 09:43.017
and give you a ride home?

09:43.310 --> 09:45.562
You know, before you freeze to death.

09:50.901 --> 09:53.486
Okay! First-time flyers, hold on tight.

09:53.863 --> 09:55.905
Appa, yip yip!

10:04.999 --> 10:06.749
Come on, Appa, yip yip.

10:07.626 --> 10:10.128
Wow, that was truly amazing.

10:10.379 --> 10:11.504
Appa's just tired.

10:11.589 --> 10:14.716
A little rest and he'll
be soaring through the sky. You'll see.

10:18.554 --> 10:20.346
Why are you smiling at me like that?

10:20.639 --> 10:22.390
I was smiling?

10:38.866 --> 10:40.617
I'm going to bed now.

10:43.412 --> 10:46.581
Yep. A man needs his rest.

10:47.750 --> 10:51.502
Prince Zuko, you need some sleep.

10:51.921 --> 10:53.796
Even if you're right,

10:53.881 --> 10:57.634
and the Avatar is alive,
you won't find him.

10:58.427 --> 11:04.307
Your father, grandfather, and
great-grandfather all tried and failed.

11:04.725 --> 11:08.186
Because their honor
didn't hinge on the Avatar's capture.

11:08.270 --> 11:09.812
Mine does.

11:09.897 --> 11:12.148
This coward's hundred years
in hiding are over.

11:23.744 --> 11:24.744
Hey.

11:25.496 --> 11:27.413
Hey. What are you thinking about?

11:27.665 --> 11:29.248
I guess I was wondering.

11:29.333 --> 11:31.167
Your being an airbender and all...

11:31.377 --> 11:33.670
If you had any idea
what happened to the Avatar.

11:34.421 --> 11:37.465
No. I didn't know him.

11:37.549 --> 11:39.717
I mean, I knew people that knew him.

11:39.802 --> 11:41.844
But I didn't. Sorry.

11:41.929 --> 11:43.471
Okay. Just curious.

11:43.847 --> 11:46.432
-Good night.
-Sleep tight.

12:31.103 --> 12:33.104
Aang. Aang, wake up!

12:34.314 --> 12:36.733
It's okay. We're in the village now.

12:36.984 --> 12:38.151
Come on, get ready.

12:38.235 --> 12:39.736
Everyone's waiting to meet you.

12:54.501 --> 12:57.503
Aang, this is the entire village.

12:58.005 --> 13:00.590
Entire village, Aang.

13:03.177 --> 13:06.596
Why are they all
looking at me like that?

13:07.139 --> 13:08.514
Did Appa sneeze on me?

13:08.766 --> 13:11.726
Well, no one has seen an airbender
in a hundred years.

13:11.935 --> 13:13.352
We thought they were extinct.

13:13.896 --> 13:16.147
Until my granddaughter
and grandson found you.

13:16.732 --> 13:18.232
Extinct?

13:18.317 --> 13:19.776
Aang, this is my grandmother.

13:20.152 --> 13:21.694
Call me Gran Gran.

13:22.863 --> 13:24.655
What is this, a weapon?

13:24.865 --> 13:26.532
You can't stab anything with this.

13:26.742 --> 13:29.786
It's not for stabbing.
It's for airbending.

13:31.413 --> 13:33.206
Magic trick, do it again!

13:33.707 --> 13:35.541
Not magic, airbending.

13:35.876 --> 13:39.045
It lets me control the air currents
around my glider and fly.

13:39.421 --> 13:41.172
You know, last time I checked,

13:41.256 --> 13:42.924
humans can't fly.

13:43.217 --> 13:44.759
Check again!

13:47.513 --> 13:49.347
Wow, he's flying.

13:53.018 --> 13:54.435
He's amazing!

13:59.775 --> 14:01.109
Unh!

14:06.448 --> 14:08.491
My watchtower.

14:12.121 --> 14:13.538
That was amazing.

14:18.961 --> 14:20.336
Great.

14:20.462 --> 14:22.630
You're an airbender,
Katara's a waterbender.

14:22.714 --> 14:25.091
Together you can just
waste time all day long.

14:25.551 --> 14:26.759
You're a waterbender!

14:27.010 --> 14:29.137
Well, sort of. Not yet.

14:29.471 --> 14:30.888
All right. No more playing.

14:31.473 --> 14:33.808
Come on, Katara. You have chores.

14:34.184 --> 14:36.686
I told you.
He's the real thing, Gran Gran.

14:36.854 --> 14:38.855
I finally found a bender to teach me.

14:39.273 --> 14:42.525
Katara, try not to put
all your hopes in this boy.

14:42.609 --> 14:44.652
But he's special. I can tell.

14:45.112 --> 14:48.156
I sense he's filled with much wisdom.

14:48.824 --> 14:52.076
See? Now my wand is stuck to my tongue.

14:59.001 --> 15:00.418
Again.

15:00.878 --> 15:03.254
Hiya!

15:04.548 --> 15:06.757
No!

15:06.842 --> 15:09.844
Power and firebending
come from the breath,

15:09.970 --> 15:11.971
not the muscles.

15:12.973 --> 15:16.184
The breath becomes energy in the body.

15:16.435 --> 15:20.855
The energy extends past your limbs
and becomes fire!

15:20.939 --> 15:22.940
Get it right this time.

15:23.275 --> 15:26.485
Enough. I've been drilling
this sequence all day.

15:26.570 --> 15:28.779
Teach me the next set.
I'm more than ready.

15:28.864 --> 15:30.406
No! You're impatient.

15:31.200 --> 15:33.492
You have yet to master your basics.

15:33.660 --> 15:34.994
Drill it again!

15:35.329 --> 15:36.579
Hiya!

15:39.082 --> 15:43.044
The sages tell us that the Avatar
is the last airbender.

15:43.128 --> 15:45.838
He must be over
a hundred years old by now.

15:45.923 --> 15:48.216
He's had a century
to master the four elements.

15:48.300 --> 15:51.510
I'll need more
than basic firebending to defeat him.

15:51.595 --> 15:54.138
You will teach me the advanced set!

15:55.682 --> 16:00.686
Very well. But first,
I must finish my roast duck.

16:01.647 --> 16:02.939
Yum, yum, yum.

16:05.067 --> 16:07.902
Now, men, it's important
that you show no fear

16:07.986 --> 16:09.487
when you face a firebender.

16:09.571 --> 16:12.990
In the Water Tribe,
we fight till the last man's standing.

16:13.075 --> 16:16.077
For without courage,
how can we call ourselves men?

16:19.039 --> 16:20.373
I gotta pee.

16:20.666 --> 16:23.334
Listen! Until your fathers
return from the war,

16:23.418 --> 16:26.045
they're counting on you
to be the men of this tribe.

16:26.129 --> 16:28.172
And that means no potty breaks.

16:28.340 --> 16:29.590
But I really gotta go.

16:31.134 --> 16:33.302
Okay. Who else has to go?

16:37.182 --> 16:39.225
Have you seen Aang?

16:39.309 --> 16:41.602
Gran Gran said
he disappeared over an hour ago.

16:42.229 --> 16:44.939
Wow! Everything freezes in there.

16:46.692 --> 16:48.401
Katara, get him out of here.

16:48.485 --> 16:50.861
This lesson is for warriors only.

16:50.946 --> 16:51.946
Wee!

16:52.030 --> 16:53.906
Ha! Ha! Ha!

16:57.035 --> 16:58.911
Stop! Stop it right now!

16:59.663 --> 17:00.997
What's wrong with you?

17:01.081 --> 17:03.749
We don't have time for fun and games
with a war going on!

17:03.875 --> 17:05.251
What war?

17:05.335 --> 17:06.711
What are you talking about?

17:06.962 --> 17:08.045
You're kidding, right?

17:09.006 --> 17:10.923
Penguin!

17:17.055 --> 17:19.223
He's kidding, right?

17:25.605 --> 17:27.440
Aang!

17:28.150 --> 17:30.318
Ha! Ha! Hey, come on, little guy.

17:30.402 --> 17:32.486
Wanna go sledding? Unh!

17:34.781 --> 17:36.407
I have a way with animals.

17:41.830 --> 17:45.374
Aang, I'll help you catch a penguin,
if you teach me waterbending.

17:46.084 --> 17:48.002
You got a deal.

17:48.253 --> 17:49.837
Just one little problem.

17:50.047 --> 17:51.839
I'm an airbender, not a waterbender.

17:51.923 --> 17:54.467
Isn't there someone
in your tribe who can teach you?

17:55.218 --> 17:59.513
No. You're looking at the only waterbender
in the whole South Pole.

17:59.681 --> 18:01.140
This isn't right.

18:01.224 --> 18:02.975
A waterbender needs to master water.

18:04.186 --> 18:05.978
What about the North Pole?

18:06.063 --> 18:08.272
There's another water tribe
up there, right?

18:08.398 --> 18:10.733
Maybe they have waterbenders
who could teach you.

18:10.817 --> 18:12.610
Maybe, but we haven't had contact

18:12.694 --> 18:15.196
with our sister tribe in a long time.

18:15.364 --> 18:18.199
It's not exactly turn right
at the second glacier.

18:18.283 --> 18:20.034
It's on the other side of the world.

18:20.160 --> 18:22.536
But you forget. I have a flying bison.

18:22.621 --> 18:26.123
Appa and I can personally
fly you to the North Pole.

18:26.208 --> 18:28.250
Katara, we're gonna find you a master.

18:28.460 --> 18:30.669
That's... I mean...

18:30.754 --> 18:33.589
I don't know. I've never left home before.

18:33.673 --> 18:35.007
Well, you think about it.

18:35.092 --> 18:38.469
But in the meantime, can you teach me
to catch one of these penguins?

18:39.346 --> 18:42.723
Okay. Listen closely, my young pupil.

18:42.808 --> 18:45.851
Catching penguins
is an ancient and sacred art.

18:46.353 --> 18:48.145
Observe.

18:51.566 --> 18:54.568
Ha! Ha! Ha! Ha!

19:03.662 --> 19:06.539
Ha! Ha! Yeah!

19:10.460 --> 19:11.710
Whoo!

19:15.715 --> 19:18.884
-I haven't done this since I was a kid.
-You still are a kid!

19:40.824 --> 19:42.199
Whoa...

19:42.826 --> 19:44.660
What is that?

19:44.870 --> 19:46.537
A Fire Navy ship,

19:46.913 --> 19:49.248
and a very bad memory for my people.

19:52.544 --> 19:53.919
Aang, stop.

19:54.004 --> 19:55.546
We're not allowed to go near it.

19:55.630 --> 19:57.256
The ship could be booby-trapped.

19:57.382 --> 20:00.009
If you want to be a bender,
you have to let go of fear.

20:47.140 --> 20:50.684
This ship has haunted my tribe
since Gran Gran was a little girl.

20:50.977 --> 20:53.354
It was part of
the Fire Nation's first attacks.

20:54.314 --> 20:55.981
Okay. Back up.

20:56.274 --> 20:57.942
I have friends all over the world,

20:58.026 --> 20:59.318
even in the Fire Nation.

20:59.402 --> 21:00.819
I've never seen any war.

21:00.946 --> 21:03.364
Aang, how long were you in that iceberg?

21:03.907 --> 21:06.492
I don't know. A few days maybe...

21:06.701 --> 21:09.495
I think it was more like a hundred years.

21:10.080 --> 21:11.664
What? That's impossible.

21:12.123 --> 21:14.333
Do I look like a 112-year-old man to you?

21:14.584 --> 21:15.626
Think about it.

21:15.710 --> 21:17.419
The war is a century old.

21:17.546 --> 21:20.589
You don't know about it, because somehow

21:20.674 --> 21:22.883
you were in there that whole time.

21:23.134 --> 21:24.969
It's the only explanation.

21:26.763 --> 21:28.681
A hundred years.

21:29.015 --> 21:30.724
I can't believe it.

21:30.809 --> 21:32.601
I'm sorry, Aang.

21:32.686 --> 21:35.563
Maybe, somehow,
there's a bright side to all this.

21:35.897 --> 21:37.273
I did get to meet you.

21:38.984 --> 21:40.818
Come on. Let's get out of here.

21:47.534 --> 21:50.286
Aang, let's head back.
This place is creepy.

21:54.291 --> 21:56.625
What's that you said about booby traps?

22:10.765 --> 22:12.016
Hold on tight!

22:23.570 --> 22:25.654
The last airbender.

22:26.323 --> 22:28.115
Quite agile for his old age.

22:29.117 --> 22:33.412
Wake my uncle!
Tell him I found the Avatar.

22:39.377 --> 22:41.295
As well as his hiding place.
